/-!
# Prime syntax for the current language-operation fragment

The semantic Data action already accepts an arbitrary structural language
route.  This module supplies the converse, syntax-first direction for the
current selected Zero/Prime region:

* primitive authored routes form a quiver;
* Mathlib's path category is the freely composed operation syntax;
* interpretation into the current GSLT-IL stage category is fully faithful;
* the same paths are encoded by declaration-aware, typed `PureTm` terms; and
* executing an encoded route uses the existing internal Data transport.

The syntax is specified without referring to the semantic action.  In
particular, there is no primitive reverse route.  Full faithfulness is proved
for the selected fragment rather than postulated by defining the fragment as
the image of the semantic map.
-/

namespace Mettapedia.Languages.MeTTa.Prime.LanguageOperationSyntax

